====================================
*LINKAGES BETWEEN ENGINE AND SCRIPTS
====================================

  Eat the one-pound burger one bite at a time. Cross these off as you go.

      C++                   LUA
      ---                   ---
  REGISTER
  ========
  \world set/get     <-  worldSet/Get    (WARNING: C++ side needs explicit wrappers for every World  subtype)
  \push dialogue     <-  pushDialogue    (WARNING: C++ side needs explicit wrappers for every Window subtype)
  push text menu    <-  pushTextMenu    (WARNING: C++ side needs explicit wrappers for every Window subtype)
  push grid         <-  pushGrid        (WARNING: C++ side needs explicit wrappers for every Window subtype)
  pop window        <-  popWindow
  strt/stop/ps/unps <-  sys  <- wrappers for easier calls (provided by bicycle)
     * timer
     * animation
     * rendering
     * motion
     * sound
     * song
  new/del time      <-  new/delTimer (returns ID)
  inflate genome    <-  inflateGenome (including scene; should automate window creation too, that'd be sweet)
  roll dice         <-  rollDice

                        FIND
                        ====
  onTrigger         -> onTrigger()
                        ----------
                        Shunts to individual entities' metamethods:
                          * onInput (global, shunts to entity-specific onInput map)
                          * onTimeout
                          * onCollision

+=======+
|TRIGGER|
+=======+
  \INPUT
  ======
    windows back in working order
      \ Dialogue back in working order
        \ Dialogue's update() needs to be moved a render() function
      \Menu back in working order
        \inherit menu to text menu
      \Grid back in working order
        \z-layers (just use vectors. It'll be okay, nobody GAF. Only change it when you absolutely need to.)
          \each layer can have a BG and FG

  \TIMER
  ======
    \ timers flow through Trigger to callback

  \COLLISION
  ==========
    \any entity, doesn't have to be in top window
    \flow through Trigger to callback

  SCRIPTING
  =========
    implement all linkages*

  ORCHESTRA
  =========
    everything flows through Trigger
    TODO distinguish onInputWindow from onInput[Entity]
    
  LOADING
  =======
    * GENOMES: loading entities from genomes and passing their IDs to lua-side
    * INFLATE: reuse inflate() from jb
    * GRAPHS:  hooking scenes together through graph

  BUMP ALLOCATOR
  ==============
    * Is this even that helpful for this engine? I suspect not.

  UNFINISHED SUBSYSTEMS
  =====================
    * motion: It seems like motion can have another function after normal pos += vel to see if entities with destinations have reached ( or passed ) them yet with edits for gone-pasts.
    * animation
    * rendering (maybe this shouldn't be a subsystem so much as a start/stop/pause/unpause of Image visibility
    * motion
    * sound
    * song

